<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia March car registration rise 1.3 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia March car registration rise 1.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian new motor vehicle registrations rose a seasonally-adjusted 1.3 percent in March to 59,321, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Economists had expected a fall of about 2.25 percent.  </p>
<p>				March 97     Feb 97   March 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    59,321     58,580     53,514</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 54,972     54,871     54,803</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  58,382     57,233     53,933</p>
<p>NOTE: The bureau said passenger vehicle registrations rose 1.1 percent in March, adjusted, while other vehicles rose 2.1 percent.</p>
<p>March registrations rose for the sixth consecutive month in trend terms, with the rate of increase remaining steady over the last three months.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
